Description: Bind N5 PRO / F8NAB read-only
 Two users report an N5 Pro whose DMI board name is F8NAB instead of
 F8NAA (product "N5 PRO", BIOS 1.04; audit-20261016 BACKLOG #52, #53).
 Without a table entry the module does not bind there unless force=1,
 and udev does not load it (no matching DMI alias).
 .
 New profile "Minisforum N5 Pro / F8NAB" and DMI entry product "N5 PRO",
 board "F8NAB", without sys_vendor in the match, as the N5 Air entries
 (the vendor string of that board is not measured). The profile is not
 in the downstream write allowlist (0002), so the board is read-only
 also with experimental_write=1 as set by the package: no PWM nodes,
 nothing touched, no write at unbind or shutdown; sensor reads still
 send EC read commands. Write access for F8NAB needs raw data from such
 a board first (#52). The probe error text lists the new board.
 .
 Not taken from the reporters' fork (#53): the global enable_write
 parameter and its semantics.
 .
 Tested: build W=1, sparse, smatch, checkpatch (befunde/raw/
 sr2-build-20261102.txt); modinfo alias contains pnN5PRO and rnF8NAB.
 Not tested on an F8NAB board (none available).
